            <div xml:id="d330">

                <pb facs="0266" n="216" xml:id="pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/264</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-01-09T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                                1918, 1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1972. Your 2184, January 3, 7 p.m., transmitted to Stevens who is now with Emerson’s party at Nagasaki. He will be instructed to return to
                    Vladivostok as soon as situation makes it practicable for him to do so.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
